      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T15:26:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, when uniform blocks are in SSBOs, they need to be sized so that each array entry can be accessed correctly in units of the struct-size. Having padding at the end of the struct to match its max alignment is consistent with how C++ does it, so should be familiar to devs. The alternative would be we calculate the padding needed each time we append a new entry, but I like having users of UniformManager and SkUniformDataBlock be relatively dumb in these regards.",
